---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import DemoDevice from '../components/DemoDevice.astro';
import { href } from '../../model.mjs';
---
<Page>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 id="hero-heading">A second brain<br/>that goes with you.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Capture a thought. Work through a decision. <br/>Follow the work.</p>
        <div class="cta-row"><a class="button" href="#demo" data-explore>Explore the demo <Arrow/></a><a class="text-link" href={href('docs/quickstart/')}>Get started <Arrow/></a></div>
        <div class="demo-controls" id="demo">
          <div class="scenarios" role="group" aria-label="Choose a demonstration scenario">
            <button type="button" data-scenario="explore" aria-pressed="false">Explore</button><button type="button" data-scenario="decide" aria-pressed="true">Decide</button><button type="button" data-scenario="work" aria-pressed="false">Follow the work</button><button type="button" data-scenario="capture" aria-pressed="false">Capture</button><button type="button" class="reset" data-reset>Reset</button>
          </div>
          <p class="demo-disclosure">Interactive demo · fictional data · staged responses</p>
          <noscript><p>The previews are real product captures. Enable JavaScript to try the staged interactions.</p></noscript><p class="demo-hint" aria-live="polite">Try it: choose your priorities, then explore the plan.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phones" aria-label="Two real Brain application views">
        <DemoDevice side="left" scene="rank" caption="Choose what matters" title="Interactive Brain demonstration: choose your priorities" />
        <DemoDevice side="right" scene="rich" theme="dark" caption="A plan you can use" title="Interactive Brain demonstration: departure plan" />
        <p class="pwa-qualification">Supported PWA features depend on host and browser setup.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="desktop-passage" aria-labelledby="desktop-heading">
      <div class="desktop-copy"><h2 id="desktop-heading">The same brain,<br/>room to think.</h2><p>Inspect the work behind your decisions. <br/>Follow agents, review tool steps, and <br/>respond when a task needs you.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button" href="#demo" data-work>Explore the demo <Arrow/></a><a class="text-link" href={href('docs/quickstart/')}>Get started <Arrow/></a></div></div>
      <DemoDevice side="desktop" scene="work" caption="Follow the work" title="Interactive Brain Actions: inspect a staged departure review" device="desktop" width={1100} height={760} lazy />
    </section>
    <section class="answer-passage" aria-labelledby="answer-heading">
      <h2 id="answer-heading">Answers you can<br/>work with.</h2>
      <div class="answer-body"><p class="section-lead">A place on a map. A comparison that makes the trade-offs clear. A question you can answer by putting your priorities in order.</p><p>Your brain can use the shape that fits the task, then act through its tools. Follow the conversation into the work, and respond when an action needs your permission.</p><div class="scenario-links"><button type="button" data-jump="explore">Explore a structured answer <Arrow/></button><button type="button" data-jump="decide">Put priorities in order <Arrow/></button><button type="button" data-jump="work">Review an archive request <Arrow/></button></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="capture-passage" aria-labelledby="capture-heading">
      <div class="capture-copy"><h2 id="capture-heading">Catch the thought.<br/>Keep moving.</h2><p class="section-lead">Review a dictated thought before it becomes part of the conversation.</p><p>A configured PWA can also receive reviewed operating-system shares, save recordings on your device and notify you when work needs attention.</p><p class="feature-limit">Host and browser support vary. Cached offline capture is limited; agent work, history and transcription need a connection.</p><button type="button" class="button" data-jump="capture">Try dictation review <Arrow/></button></div>
      <DemoDevice side="capture" scene="voice" caption="Staged dictation · no microphone access" title="Brain dictation review: edit a staged thought before sending" device="capture" width={390} height={660} lazy zoomable={false} />
    </section>
    <section class="foundation-passage" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="foundation-heading">
      <div><h2 id="foundation-heading">Built on files.<br/>Built for you.</h2><p class="section-lead">Your knowledge lives in Markdown, in your own repository.</p><p>The agent operates on those files. Search helps it find context; tools and skills let it do useful work. The SQLite index is disposable and can be rebuilt from the source.</p><p>Use the UI, a coding agent or the command line. Choose your model and voice providers, with their own costs and data policies.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('docs/concepts/')}>Understand the foundation <Arrow/></a></div>
      <div class="file-example"><p>Fictional example · Odysseus</p><pre><code># Leaving Ogygia

The raft is ready to launch.

Departure: 2026-07-12
Planned passage: 17 days
Planned landfall: Scheria

Prepare water and provisions.
Review Calypso’s sailing directions.</code></pre><p>Readable files. Versioned with git. Yours to keep.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-heading"><h2 id="closing-heading">Make it your<br/>second brain.</h2><div><p class="section-lead">Start with your own repository and the canonical quickstart.</p><p>The UI packages are published. The hosting starter is still in development; this is a toolkit for your own brain, rather than a hosted account.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button" href={href('docs/quickstart/')}>Get started <Arrow/></a><a class="text-link" href={href('docs/hosting/')}>Explore the UI setup <Arrow/></a></div></div></section>
  </main>
  <script>
    import { initializeDemoDevices } from '../scripts/demo-devices';
    const scenarios = {
      decide: { left: 'rank', right: 'rich', captions: ['Choose what matters', 'A plan you can use'], hint: 'Try it: choose your priorities, then explore the plan.' },
      explore: { left: 'comparison', right: 'files', captions: ['Make the trade-offs visible', 'Follow the related records'], hint: 'Try it: open the frontmatter, follow a related note, or browse the Odyssey in Files. Ask for “crew ledger” to explore a table.' },
      work: { left: 'work', right: 'approval', captions: ['Follow the work', 'Respond when you’re needed'], hint: 'Try it: inspect a recorded run, then approve or deny the staged archive.' },
      capture: { left: 'voice', right: 'rich', captions: ['Review before sending', 'Continue with your brain'], hint: 'Try it: edit the staged dictation and send it. No microphone is used.' },
    };
    let current: keyof typeof scenarios = 'decide';
    const frames = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLIFrameElement>('iframe[data-demo]')];
    function select(key: keyof typeof scenarios, reset = false) {
      current = key; const scenario = scenarios[key];
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-scenario]').forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.scenario === key)));
      for (const side of ['left', 'right'] as const) {
        const frame = frames.find(frame => frame.dataset.side === side);
        if (frame) frame.dataset.pendingScene = scenario[side];
        frame?.contentWindow?.postMessage({ type: 'brain-demo-scene', scene: scenario[side], reset }, location.origin);
        frame?.setAttribute('title', `Interactive Brain demonstration: ${scenario.captions[side === 'left' ? 0 : 1]}`);
        document.getElementById(`${side}-caption`)!.textContent = scenario.captions[side === 'left' ? 0 : 1];
        const zoom = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`[data-open=${side}]`);
        if (zoom?.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true') zoom?.setAttribute('aria-label', `Expand ${scenario.captions[side === 'left' ? 0 : 1].toLowerCase()} demonstration`);
      }
      document.querySelector('.demo-hint')!.textContent = scenario.hint;
      if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        document.querySelector('.phones')?.animate([
          { opacity: .75, transform: 'translateY(5px)', filter: 'blur(1px)' },
          { opacity: 1, transform: 'translateY(0)', filter: 'blur(0)' },
        ], { duration: 220, easing: 'cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)' });
      }
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-scenario]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => select(button.dataset.scenario as keyof typeof scenarios)));
    document.querySelector('[data-reset]')?.addEventListener('click', () => select(current, true));
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-work]').forEach(link => link.addEventListener('click', () => select('work')));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-jump]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      select(button.dataset.jump as keyof typeof scenarios);
      document.getElementById('demo')!.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start', behavior: 'auto' });
    }));
    window.addEventListener('message', event => {
      if (event.origin !== location.origin || !frames.some(frame => frame.contentWindow === event.source)) return;
      if (event.data?.type === 'brain-demo-ready') {
        const frame = frames.find(frame => frame.contentWindow === event.source)!;
        if (frame.dataset.pendingScene) frame.contentWindow?.postMessage({ type: 'brain-demo-scene', scene: frame.dataset.pendingScene }, location.origin);
      }
      if (event.data?.type === 'brain-demo-status' && typeof event.data.message === 'string') document.querySelector('.demo-hint')!.textContent = event.data.message;
    });
    initializeDemoDevices();
  </script>
</Page>
